# Lennard-Jones melting — reference implementation.
#
# Reference for task construction and controlled comparison. NOT the unique
# correct answer: fix ids, ordering and naming may differ in a passing script.
#
# The critical detail is line 6: `lattice fcc 0.8442` takes the reduced NUMBER
# DENSITY, not a lattice constant. LAMMPS converts it, a = (4/rho*)^(1/3) =
# 1.6796. Writing 1.6796 here would build a system ~10x too dilute.

units           lj
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p

lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0

pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0 2.5

velocity        all create 1.2 87287 loop geom
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    delay 0 every 20 check no

fix             1 all nve
timestep        0.005
thermo          100
thermo_style    custom step temp pe ke etotal press
run             2000
